# Deployment

Spec: `docs/10-deployment.md`. Keep that doc in sync with any change to these files.

- One VPS, full repo checkout. `pnpm build` then `pnpm start` (`next start`) against the installed `node_modules`.
- PM2: `awx-fx-target-payment` (`npm start -- --port 3002`) and exactly one `awx-fx-worker` (`npm run worker`, `kill_timeout` 60s). Never scale the worker.
- Redis and Mongo listen on localhost only (or Mongo is Atlas). Caddy is the only public listener (80/443).
- Redis: `appendonly yes`, `maxmemory-policy noeviction` (required by BullMQ), `requirepass`, `bind 127.0.0.1`.
- Caddy: `flush_interval -1` and no read timeout for `/api/stream`; the Airwallex webhook IP allowlist on `/api/webhooks/airwallex`; an upload body limit. Proxy to `127.0.0.1:3002`.
- `TZ=UTC` on the host. Business time zones come from `AIRWALLEX_ACCOUNT_TZ`.
- `/api/health` returns 200 only when the Mongo ping, the Redis ping, a fresh `worker:heartbeat` and an Airwallex token are all OK.
- New env vars go into `.env.example`, the zod env schema, `docs/02` §8 and `docs/10` §7 together. `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` values are build-time.
- `.env` lives only on the server and is never committed.
